DATA CLEANING QUESTIONS – RAW_DATASET.CSV

  ---------------------------------
  SECTION A: COLUMN NAME CLEANING
  ---------------------------------

1.  Identify column names containing leading/trailing spaces.
2.  Detect inconsistent capitalization in column headers.
3.  Rename ‘irst Name’ to ‘First Name’.
4.  Convert all column names to snake_case format.

  ---------------------------------
  SECTION B: DATA TYPE VALIDATION
  ---------------------------------

5.  Print data types of all columns.
6.  Identify columns incorrectly typed as object but should be numeric
    or datetime.
7.  Convert the ‘Age’ column (which contains values like 10/28/2019) to
    datetime.
8.  Assuming ‘Age’ represents date of birth, compute age_years.
9.  Identify invalid date entries and handle them.

  ----------------------------
  SECTION C: SALARY CLEANING
  ----------------------------

10. Convert ‘SALARY’ from currency strings (e.g., $92.32) to float.
11. Identify rows where salary conversion fails.
12. Detect missing or malformed salary values.
13. Compute minimum, maximum, and average salary after cleaning.
14. Flag salaries equal to zero or negative.

  --------------------------
  SECTION D: NAME CLEANING
  --------------------------

15. Remove leading/trailing spaces from names.
16. Convert names to proper title case.
17. Detect names containing digits or special characters.
18. Create a full_name column combining First Name and Last name.

  ----------------------------------------
  SECTION E: EMAIL CLEANING & VALIDATION
  ----------------------------------------

19. Convert all emails to lowercase.
20. Remove leading/trailing spaces in email column.
21. Identify missing email addresses.
22. Detect duplicate emails.
23. Validate email format using regex.
24. Extract email domain and compute frequency of each domain.

  -----------------------------
  SECTION F: ADDRESS CLEANING
  -----------------------------

25. Identify addresses containing ‘P.O. Box’.
26. Detect inconsistent abbreviations (Rd. vs Road, St. vs Street).
27. Concatenate Address1, Address2, and Address3 into full_address.
28. Detect duplicate addresses.

  ----------------------------------------
  SECTION G: MISSING VALUES & DUPLICATES
  ----------------------------------------

29. Compute total missing values per column.
30. Calculate percentage of missing values.
31. Remove fully duplicate rows.
32. Identify soft duplicates (same email but different name).

  ------------------------------------
  SECTION H: DATA CONSISTENCY CHECKS
  ------------------------------------

33. Check for unrealistic ages (negative or greater than 100).
34. Detect salary outliers using IQR method.
35. Determine whether email can serve as a primary key.

  -------------------------------
  SECTION I: EXPORT & REPORTING
  -------------------------------

36. Export cleaned dataset as cleaned_dataset.csv.
37. Create a data quality report summarizing:
    -   Rows before cleaning
    -   Rows after cleaning
    -   Duplicates removed
    -   Invalid emails detected
    -   Salary conversion issues
    -   Date parsing issues
